with 24 million customers across seven  countries sky by any definition is a  massive company but this industry leader  is now pledging to improve its  environmental impact dramatically over  the next decade the media company plans  to go net zero carbon by 2030 to help in  the fight against climate change  launching our ambition to become Net  Zero Carbon by 2030 so we know that the  UK's got a target to become a net zero  by 2050 we want to do that 20 years  early and really be part of the  forefront of that move to a net zero  carbon economy the pledge is hugely  ambitious and will involve cutting  emissions created by people using sky  services like Sky TV it also plans to  reduce emissions in the workplace by  amongst other things improving transport  for its staff eventually Sky's entire  fleet of 5,000 vehicles will be switched  to zero emissions but the biggest target  will be helping the 11,000 companies  that work with Sky in its supply chain  by this Factory in China go net zero  carbon sky is already carbon neutral and  has been since 2006 as it expanded its  main campus in West London it put in  place environmentally friendly  infrastructure but its latest plan goes  far beyond this and it's hoping to  encourage others to follow its lead and  change their environmental behavior  there is no Doubt's environmental  awareness is good for business  activists like Greta tunberg have forced  the issue into public consciousness  companies like Microsoft have already  decided to move with the times it wants  to remove from the environment all the  carbon the companies emitted since its  founding in 1975 environmental experts  say it's good companies are taking the  initiative but the government needs to  do more Sky Microsoft they've all sat  down and they've looked at the science  and they've gone this is scary we need  to do this as quick as possible we can  show leadership and we can do this by  2030 now what I'm hoping is those  companies can show that if they're going  to do it then government has to follow  sky has been campaigning for the  environments for more than a decade  it's Ocean Rescue project exposed the  toxic levels of pollution in the world's  oceans and highlighted the need to pass  on single-use plastic it's hoping its  latest pledge will also inspire others  this time to go zero  Alex Rossi Sky News West London
 

